# Always deploy after changes

When finishing implementable work in this User Management / Employee Portal repo, **deploy** unless the user says not to.

## Target

- Firebase project: `master-user-management`
- Production URL: https://employee.countrylion.co.uk
- Hosting URL: https://master-user-management.web.app

## Deploy steps

1. `npm run build` in `frontend/`
2. Prefer targeted deploys to avoid deleting remote-only orphans (`clearEmergencyPhoneAssignment`, `setEmergencyPhoneAssignment`, `trutacProxy`):
   - `firebase deploy --only hosting --project master-user-management`
   - `firebase deploy --only functions:<changedFn>,... --project master-user-management` for changed/new functions
3. If a full `functions` deploy aborts on orphaned remote functions, do **not** use `--force` (that deletes them). Use targeted function deploys instead.
4. After creating new hosting rewrites for new functions, redeploy hosting once those functions exist.

## After deploy

Tell the user the live URLs for what changed (e.g. `/dashboard/cases`).
